{"step_index":221,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T14:40:34Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T18:40:34+04:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T18:40:35+04:00\nFile Path: `file:///home/koby/.gemini/antigravity-cli/brain/4cb12149-1140-450b-b195-316320800a2b/.system_generated/steps/203/output.txt`\nTotal Lines: 92\nTotal Bytes: 4339\nShowing lines 1 to 92\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Excalidraw Diagram Design Guide\n2: \n3: ## Color Palette\n4: \n5: ### Stroke Colors (use for borders & text)\n6: | Name    | Hex       | Use for                     |\n7: |---------|-----------|-----------------------------|\n8: | Black   | #1e1e1e   | Default text & borders      |\n9: | Red     | #e03131   | Errors, warnings, critical  |\n10: | Green   | #2f9e44   | Success, approved, healthy  |\n11: | Blue    | #1971c2   | Primary actions, links      |\n12: | Purple  | #9c36b5   | Services, middleware        |\n13: | Orange  | #e8590c   | Async, queues, events       |\n14: | Cyan    | #0c8599   | Data stores, databases      |\n15: | Gray    | #868e96   | Annotations, secondary      |\n16: \n17: ### Fill Colors (use for backgroundColor — pastel fills)\n18: | Name         | Hex       | Pairs with stroke |\n19: |--------------|-----------|-------------------|\n20: | Light Red    | #ffc9c9   | #e03131           |\n21: | Light Green  | #b2f2bb   | #2f9e44           |\n22: | Light Blue   | #a5d8ff   | #1971c2           |\n23: | Light Purple | #eebefa   | #9c36b5           |\n24: | Light Orange | #ffd8a8   | #e8590c           |\n25: | Light Cyan   | #99e9f2   | #0c8599           |\n26: | Light Gray   | #e9ecef   | #868e96           |\n27: | White        | #ffffff   | #1e1e1e           |\n28: \n29: ## Sizing Rules\n30: \n31: - **Minimum shape size**: width >= 120px, height >= 60px; width >= labelChars * 12 keeps labels on one line\n32: - **Solid fills**: set `fillStyle: \"solid\"` for crisp flat fills — the default hachure pattern looks sketchy\n33: - **Font sizes**: body text >= 16, titles/headers >= 20, small labels >= 14\n34: - **Padding**: leave at least 20px inside shapes for text breathing room\n35: - **Arrow length**: minimum 80px between connected shapes (120px+ when the arrow has a label)\n36: - **Consistent sizing**: keep same-role shapes identical dimensions\n37: \n38: ## Layout Patterns\n39: \n40: - **Grid snap**: align to 20px grid for clean layouts\n41: - **Spacing**: 40–80px gap between adjacent shapes\n42: - **Flow direction**: top-to-bottom (vertical) or left-to-right (horizontal)\n43: - **Hierarchy**: important nodes larger or higher; left-to-right = temporal order\n44: - **Grouping**: cluster related elements visually; use background rectangles as zones\n45: \n46: ## Arrow Binding Best Practices\n47: \n48: - **Always bind**: use `startElementId` / `endElementId` to connect arrows to shapes\n49: - **Dashed arrows**: use `strokeStyle: \"dashed\"` for async, optional, or event flows\n50: - **Dotted arrows**: use `strokeStyle: \"dotted\"` for weak dependencies or annotations\n51: - **Arrowheads**: default \"arrow\" for directed flow; \"dot\" for data stores; null for lines\n52: - **Label arrows**: set `text` on arrows to describe the relationship (e.g., \"HTTP\", \"publishes\")\n53: \n54: ## Diagram Type Templates\n55: \n56: ### Architecture Diagram\n57: - Shapes: 160×80 rectangles for services, 120×60 for small components\n58: - Colors: different fill per layer (frontend=blue, backend=purple, data=cyan)\n59: - Arrows: solid for sync calls, dashed for async/events\n60: - Zones: large light-gray background rectangles with 20px fontSize labels\n61: \n62: ### Flowchart\n63: - Shapes: 140×70 rectangles for steps, 100×100 diamonds for decisions\n64: - Flow: top-to-bottom, 60px vertical spacing\n65: - Colors: green start, red end, blue for process steps\n66: - Arrows: solid, with \"Yes\"/\"No\" labels from diamonds\n67: \n68: ### ER Diagram\n69: - Shapes: 180×40 per entity (wider for attribute lists)\n70: - Layout: 80px between entities\n71: - Arrows: use start/end arrowheads to show cardinality\n72: - Colors: light-blue fill for entities, no fill for junction tables\n73: \n74: ## Anti-Patterns to Avoid\n75: \n76: 1. **Overlapping elements** — always leave gaps; use distribute_elements\n77: 2. **Cramped spacing** — minimum 40px between shapes\n78: 3. **Tiny fonts** — never below 14px; prefer 16+\n79: 4. **Manual arrow coordinates** — always use startElementId/endElementId binding\n80: 5. **Too many colors** — limit to 3–4 fill colors per diagram\n81: 6. **Inconsistent sizes** — same-role shapes should be same width/height\n82: 7. **No labels** — every shape and meaningful arrow should have text\n83: 8. **Flat layouts** — use zones/groups to create visual hierarchy\n84: \n85: ## Drawing Order (Recommended)\n86: \n87: 1. **Background zones** — large rectangles with light fill, low opacity\n88: 2. **Primary shapes** — services, entities, steps (with labels via `text`)\n89: 3. **Arrows** — connect shapes using binding IDs\n90: 4. **Annotations** — standalone text elements for notes, titles\n91: 5. **Refinement** — align, distribute, adjust spacing, screenshot to verify\n92: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n"}
{"step_index":222,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T14:40:35Z","thinking":"Service rectangle dimensions must adhere to the specified minimum width of 160 and height of 80. Color assignments are now clear: frontend uses a specific blue, reverse proxy green, backend uses purple, caches/queues use orange, and databases are assigned a teal color. Arrows will visually represent binding relationships between the different service rectangles.\n\n\nA title element is required to label the diagram. The ingress layer consists of client browsers and a reverse proxy, each rendered as rectangles. The service layer includes authentication and core application backend services, also represented as rectangles. The data layer features a cache/session store and a database, visualized as an ellipse and a rectangle, respectively. Finally, arrows will depict the relationships between components, starting with the client to the reverse proxy.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"call_mcp_tool","args":{"Arguments":{},"ServerName":"excalidraw","ToolName":"clear_canvas","toolAction":"Clearing canvas","toolSummary":"Clear canvas before building"}}]}
