{"step_index":261,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T14:53:52Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nPlease add this doc for me? Qmail → Postfix/Dovecot Migration — Outremer Telecom\n\nStatus: In progress (pilot domain phase)\nLast updated: 2026-09-22\n\n1. Project Overview\n\nOutremer Telecom operates mail service across three regional sites — Martinique (mtq), Guadeloupe (gua), and Guyane (guy) — each running a legacy qmail-ldap stack with its own local LDAP directory. The goal is to migrate all mail service to a single, unified Postfix + Dovecot + Roundcube platform (mtq-mailsrvp-01), retiring the legacy qmail servers over time.\n\nStrategy: domain-by-domain migration rather than a single cutover, starting with the smallest, cleanest domain as a pilot before tackling larger, riskier domains.\n\nArchitecture decision: during the transition, the existing LDAP directories are not migrated or copied. Dovecot authenticates directly against the existing source LDAP over the network, using a dedicated, read-only service account. This keeps qmail and Postfix reading from a single, unchanged source of truth throughout the migration — avoiding divergent copies of account data and enabling a simple rollback if needed.\n\n2. Infrastructure Map\n\n┌─────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────┬────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│     Server      │                      Role                       │ Real account count │                                                                  Notes                                                                   │\n├─────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ smtp-mtq-1      │ Martinique qmail-ldap source                    │ 64,492             │ Scheduled for full decommission once qmail is retired                                                                                    │\n├─────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ smtp-guy-1      │ Guyane qmail-ldap source                        │ 121,461            │ Near-identical data to gua                                                                                                               │\n├─────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ smtp-gua-1      │ Guadeloupe qmail-ldap source                    │ 121,455            │ Near-identical data to guy; no native LDAP replication found (no syncrepl/contextCSN) between them — likely application-level dual-write │\n├─────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 172.30.37.225   │ LDAP server, matches guy/gua's data fingerprint │ 121,858            │ Likely the true upstream source for guy/gua; confirmed unrelated to mtq's dataset                                                        │\n├─────────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────┼────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ mtq-mailsrvp-01 │ Target Postfix/Dovecot/Roundcube platform       │ —                  │ Already hosts other live Postfix virtual domains via a separate flat-file auth mechanism                                                 │\n└─────────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────┴────────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n\nImportant methodology note: standard ldapsearch queries against these directories silently cap at 500 results (server-side size limit), which produced badly wrong early estimates. Accurate counts require slapcat (direct database read, bypasses the LDAP protocol limit).\n\n3. Key Data-Quality Findings\n\n- mail attribute corruption: some entries store a malformed double-@ address (e.g. user@domainA@domainB) — a genuine source data defect, not a search artifact.\n- Legacy webmail Sent-folder format: a non-standard flat-file format (sentmail-<pid>.<timestamp>) from a 2012–2014-era webmail application affects 59,486 files across mtq alone — a systemic issue requiring a dedicated conversion step (not a one-off fix) before these folders are visible in the new IMAP structure.\n- accountStatus is not uniform: across all 64,492 mtq accounts, only two values exist — active (64,491) and enabled (1 account) — both must be treated as valid/eligible for login.\n- Password hashing: userPassword uses the {SHA} scheme (unsalted SHA-1) consistently, which Dovecot supports natively — no password resets required for end users.\n- Two Maildir path conventions coexist: d1/<first-letter>/<user> (older) and d2/<numeric-bucket>/<user> (newer) — any migration tooling must handle both.\n- smtp-mtq-1 will be fully powered off once qmail is decommissioned. LDAP (slapd) currently runs on that same box — it will need to be relocated to a surviving host before that decommission, as a distinct, separate task.\n\n4. Pilot Domain: ool.fr\n\nSelected over two other small-domain candidates after closer inspection:\n- rife.re (3 accounts) — rejected: all accounts are deliveryMode: forwardonly (pure mail forwards, no real mailbox to migrate).\n- business.ool.fr (270 accounts on mtq) — rejected: contains known mail attribute corruption.\n- ool.fr (12 accounts) — selected: clean data, real mailboxes, ~80% concentrated on a single physical mail host.\n\n5. Current Status by Phase\n\n┌───────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ Phase │                                                       Description                                                       │                                                  Status                                                  │\n├───────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 1     │ Confirm auth architecture (Dovecot reads existing LDAP directly)                                                        │ ✅ Done                                                                                                  │\n├───────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 2     │ Map required LDAP attributes to Dovecot fields                                                                          │ ✅ Done                                                                                                  │\n├───────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 3     │ Create dedicated read-only LDAP bind account (cn=dovecot-auth,ou=services,o=ool)                                        │ ✅ Done                                                                                                  │\n├───────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 4     │ Define auth filter logic (status whitelist + forward-only exclusion), validated against the full 64,492-account dataset │ ✅ Done                                                                                                  │\n├───────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ 5     │ Wire LDAP passdb/userdb into Dovecot's auth configuration                                                               │ 🔶 In progress — blocked on Dovecot 2.4's substantially redesigned LDAP configuration syntax (see below) │\n├───────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────�